---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/calculator.css';
---
<Layout title="Disclosure Gap Calculator" description="Compare the tone, uncertainty, and readability of two disclosures. A free, browser-based research and teaching tool by M. R. Hoque.">
<div class="wrap calculator">
  <a class="back-link" href="/projects/">← All projects</a>
  <header class="calc-intro"><p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH TOOLS · VERSION 1.0</p><h1>Disclosure Gap Calculator</h1><p class="calc-lead">Two disclosures. A clearer view of the differences.</p><p>Compare an earnings call with a filing, or two versions of the same report. See exactly which words drive the results.</p><div class="calc-meta"><span>Runs in your browser</span><span>No text uploads or storage</span><a href="#methods">How it works ↓</a><a href="https://github.com/rezoanhoque/rezoanhoque.github.io/tree/main/source/src/lib">GitHub ↗</a></div></header>
  <noscript><p class="notice">Enable JavaScript to run this calculator. All analysis takes place in your browser.</p></noscript>
  <form id="calculator-form">
    <div class="calc-toolbar"><p><strong>01</strong> Add your disclosures</p><div><button type="button" id="example">Load fictional example</button><button type="button" id="swap">Swap A / B</button><button type="button" id="clear">Clear</button></div></div>
    <div class="input-grid">
      {['A','B'].map((side)=><section class="input-panel"><label class="text-label" for={`text-${side}`}><span class="side-badge">{side}</span> Disclosure {side}</label><p>{side==='A'?'For example: earnings-call remarks':'For example: 10-K MD&A'}</p><textarea id={`text-${side}`} maxlength="200000" rows="11" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Paste English disclosure text here…" required aria-describedby={`count-${side}`}></textarea><div class="input-footer"><label class="file-label">Open .txt<input type="file" id={`file-${side}`} accept=".txt,text/plain" /></label><span id={`count-${side}`}>0 / 200,000 characters</span></div></section>)}
    </div>
    <details class="dictionary-panel"><summary>Word lists <span id="dictionary-label">Illustrative starter lists · not LM</span></summary><p>The starter lists demonstrate the method and are not a validated financial sentiment dictionary. Edit them below or import the official Loughran–McDonald master CSV for research use.</p><div class="dictionary-actions"><label class="file-label">Import LM CSV<input type="file" id="dictionary-file" accept=".csv,text/csv" /></label><button type="button" id="reset-dictionary">Restore starter lists</button><a href="https://sraf.nd.edu/loughranmcdonald-master-dictionary/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Get the LM dictionary ↗</a></div><div class="lexicon-grid">{['positive','negative','uncertainty'].map(cat=><label>{cat}<textarea id={`lexicon-${cat}`} rows="4" spellcheck="false"></textarea></label>)}</div><p>Exact word matches; no stemming or negation adjustment. “Not strong” still counts “strong.”</p></details>
    <div class="run-row"><button class="btn btn-primary" id="calculate" type="submit">Compare disclosures →</button><span>All gaps are A minus B.</span></div><p id="error" role="alert" hidden></p>
  </form>
  <section id="results" hidden aria-labelledby="results-heading" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="calc-toolbar"><h2 id="results-heading">Your comparison</h2><button type="button" id="download">Download results (JSON) ↓</button></div>
    <p id="result-note" class="notice"></p><div class="metric-grid" id="metrics"></div>
    <div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Underlying measurements · positive gaps mean A is higher</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Measure</th><th scope="col">Disclosure A</th><th scope="col">Disclosure B</th><th scope="col">A − B</th></tr></thead><tbody id="measurements"></tbody></table></div>
    <div class="input-grid matched-grid"><section><h3>Matched words · A</h3><div id="matches-A"></div></section><section><h3>Matched words · B</h3><div id="matches-B"></div></section></div>
  </section>
  <section id="methods" class="methods"><p class="eyebrow">TRANSPARENT BY DESIGN</p><h2>What the numbers mean</h2><div class="method-grid"><div><h3>Tone &amp; uncertainty</h3><p>Each category counts matching word occurrences, divided by all word tokens and multiplied by 100. Net tone is the positive rate minus the negative rate. Tone and uncertainty gaps are percentage-point differences: A − B.</p><p>These are descriptive text measures, not evidence of deception, a forecast, or an investment recommendation. Compare similar sections and periods; quotations, negation, context, and document length can change interpretation.</p></div><div><h3>Readability</h3><p>We report average words per sentence and the Automated Readability Index (ARI): 4.71 × characters/words + 0.5 × words/sentences − 21.43. A higher ARI indicates greater estimated reading difficulty; it does not measure disclosure quality. We retain raw scores, including negative values.</p><p><a href="https://tsapps.nist.gov/publication/get_pdf.cfm?pub_id=914701">ARI formula reference (NIST) ↗</a></p></div></div><details><summary>Counting rules, limits, and reproducibility</summary><p>English text only. Text is Unicode-normalized (NFKC) and lowercased. Tokens are English letter sequences (internal apostrophes retained) or numbers (decimal/comma groups retained); hyphens split words. Numbers enter the denominator. ARI characters are token letters and digits. English Intl.Segmenter detects sentences, so abbreviations and browser versions may affect counts. No stop words are removed. Inputs are limited to 200,000 characters each; short passages below 100 words are flagged.</p><p>LM imports use category values strictly greater than zero; negative removal-year flags are excluded. Categories may overlap. Exports contain exact word lists, all calculated measurements, version, and input SHA-256 fingerprints, but exclude the original texts. Keep your original texts to reproduce a comparison.</p><p>Text and imported dictionaries stay in memory in this browser tab. Editing an input hides old results until you calculate again. Nothing is saved to local storage. The theme preference is stored separately by the portfolio.</p></details><p class="method-footer">Built by M. R. Hoque · <a href="https://github.com/rezoanhoque/rezoanhoque.github.io/blob/main/source/DISCLOSURE_CALCULATOR.md">Documentation &amp; source</a> · <a href="mailto:mrezoan1@lsuneworleans.edu?subject=Disclosure%20Gap%20Calculator%20feedback">Send feedback</a></p></section>
</div><script src="../../scripts/calculator.ts"></script>
</Layout>
